{"insertText":{"location":{"index":144577,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"text":"\nTwo rules apply to every comparison below. First, ROC-AUC differences are paired: both models are evaluated on the same videos, and each bootstrap draw or permutation is applied to both. Intervals are 95% percentile intervals from 5,000 stratified cluster-bootstrap draws and are not adjusted for multiplicity, so the decision for each comparison is the Holm-adjusted p-value of the rank-based cluster permutation test; Holm-adjusted p-values below 0.005, which include the smallest attainable values, are written as < 0.005. Second, the inference is conditional on the trained ensembles: it describes how the evaluated models perform on new test videos, not how a retrained model would perform. Threshold-independent results (ROC-AUC and PR-AUC) and threshold-dependent results (accuracy, precision, recall, specificity, and F1-score) are reported separately, and differences in threshold-dependent metrics are given only as supplementary paired intervals, without tests."}},
{"updateParagraphStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":144578,"endIndex":145551,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"JUSTIFIED","lineSpacing":200,"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"spaceAbove":{"magnitude":0,"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"magnitude":0,"unit":"PT"},"keepWithNext":false},"fields":"namedStyleType,alignment,lineSpacing,indentFirstLine,spaceAbove,spaceBelow,keepWithNext"}},
